sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant AuthorService
    participant AuthorRepository
    participant Database
    participant Author

    Client->>AuthorService: updateauthor(author)
    Note right of Client: Client calls AuthorService.update with Author object

    AuthorService->>AuthorService: findById(author.getId())
    Note right of AuthorService: AuthorService calls findById to retrieve existing author

    AuthorService->>AuthorRepository: findById(id)

    AuthorRepository->>Database: SELECT * FROM authors WHERE id = ?

    Database-->>Author: return existing Author
    Note right of Database: Existing Author object from database

    AuthorRepository-->>AuthorService: return Author

    alt Author found
        AuthorService->>Author: updateData(newAuthor)
        Note right of AuthorService: Transfer new values from input author to existing author

        Author->>Author: this.name = newAuthor.getName()
        Note right of Author: Update name field

        Author->>Author: this.email = newAuthor.getEmail()
        Note right of Author: Update email field

        AuthorService->>AuthorRepository: save(updatedAuthor)

        AuthorRepository->>Database: UPDATE authors SET ... WHERE id = ?
        Note right of AuthorRepository: Database updated with new values

        Database-->>Author: return updated Author
        Note right of Database: Updated Author object

        AuthorRepository-->>AuthorService: return Author
        Note right of AuthorRepository: Updated Author returned to service

        AuthorService-->>Client: return Author
        Note right of AuthorService: Updated Author returned to client

    else Author not found
        AuthorService->>AuthorService: throw ObjectNotFoundException
        Note right of AuthorService: ObjectNotFoundException if author does not exist

        AuthorService-->>Client: ObjectNotFoundException propagates
        Note right of AuthorService: Exception propagates to caller
    end
